    "feedback": [
      {
        "math_academy_id": "question-017",
        "problem": "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+25y=24\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(25t+\u03d5)+12\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t+\u03d5)+6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20615t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20615t+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R$ and $\u03d5$ are constants.",
        "worked_solution": "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{\u2033}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$ It can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=25\\,\u27f9\\,\\omega =5.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20615t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20615t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =1$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t+\u03d5)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t+\u03d5)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u20615t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u20615t+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n\nOnly III matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
        "deliberately_incorrect_submission": false,
        "submitted_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
